# Make a rogue and get into the dungeon.
#
# The character is a male orc rogue, neutral, worshipping whichever god the
# game offers. The race is the same orc the other chargen scripts use, on
# purpose: only the class-specific part of this file differs from chargen.keys,
# so only that part can rot.
#
# Why a rogue: the game's own class screen calls rogue the flavour of
# character that exercises the skill system, and the skill system is what a
# barbarian walk never touches. A rogue starts with fourteen skill ranks
# against the barbarian's five, so searching, hiding and moving silently
# actually resolve instead of failing on every roll.
#
# The race, subrace, class and alignment are named, not counted, so a race or
# class added to lib/ cannot make this script build a different character.
# See @choose in src/Wposix.cpp. Run with a fixed seed all the same
# (tools/headless.sh <script> <seed>): the attribute rolls decide which feats
# the game offers, and the two feat picks below are still positional.

a       # Initial Choices: [a] Create a New Character
n       # Alter the character generation options? -- no
y       # Your options will place the game in Explore Mode. Continue? -- yes
@choose "Orc"
@choose "Orc (Standard)"
@choose "Rogue"
a       # Attributes: the first of the five offered sets. The sets have no
        #   names, so this one stays positional.
@choose "Neutral"   # This is why the alignment is named. A barbarian may not
                    #   be lawful, so chargen.keys sees a shortened list of six
                    #   and Neutral falls on [c]; a rogue sees the full nine
                    #   and it falls on [e]. The name is the same on both.
a       # First feat.  Which feats are offered depends on the attribute
a       # Second feat. rolls, so these two stay counted.

# Skill Manager. RIGHT spends a rank on the selected skill and stops at the
# skill's maximum, DOWN moves to the next skill, so three RIGHTs per skill
# spends everything available without needing to know how many ranks this
# character has. Twelve skills at two ranks each covers the rogue's fourteen
# ranks with room to spare. Character generation will not let go until the
# pool is empty.
RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN
RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN
ENTER y # Done, and confirm keeping the ranks

y       # Do you wish to worship <god>? -- yes
        #   A rogue gains no second pool of skill ranks from the choice of
        #   god, so no second Skill Manager pass follows here.

a       # Personality archetype

# A rogue learns no spells, so generation ends here.
# The next keystroke dismisses the arrival room description and lands in the
# dungeon, in play mode.
